.TH "SCCFM-CLI INVENTORY DEVICES ASA SHUN SHOW" "1" "2026-07-27" "0.38.0" "sccfm-cli inventory devices asa shun show Manual"
.SH NAME
sccfm-cli\-inventory\-devices\-asa\-shun\-show \- Display active shun entries on ASA devices.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sccfm-cli inventory devices asa shun show
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Display active shun entries on ASA devices. Use --statistics for per-interface counters.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n,\fP \-\-device\-name TEXT
Device name to search for (supports wildcards like 'branch-*').
.TP
\fB\-q,\fP \-\-query TEXT
Filter devices by a Lucene query.
.TP
\fB\-l,\fP \-\-limit INTEGER RANGE
Maximum records to return  [default: 50; 1<=x<=200]
.TP
\fB\-o,\fP \-\-offset INTEGER RANGE
Pagination offset  [default: 0; x>=0]
.TP
\fB\-u,\fP \-\-device\-uids TEXT
List of device UIDs to view shuns on.
.TP
\fB\-\-statistics\fP
Show per-interface shun statistics instead of shun entries.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP [table|json]
Output format  [default: table]
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-path\fP PATH
Path to the configuration file (defaults to ~/.sccfm-cli/config.json).
